blocks.en:
For the pair form, we show 5 pairs at a time;
for the group form, we use a larger window of 40 questions at a time (20 hard and 20 easy);
For both prompting formats, we provide the question text, its reference answer, and its difficulty b b for every question shown.
Although the two forms are intended to capture different granularities, we explicitly instruct the model in both cases to avoid generating overly specific hypotheses.
See our prompt templates in Appendix B .

blocks.zh:
对于配对形式,我们一次显示5对;
对于组合形式,我们每次使用40个问题(20个硬和20个简单)的大窗口;
对于两种提示格式,我们提供问题文本、其参考答案和每个问题的困难bb。
虽然这两种形式旨在捕捉不同的颗粒,但我们明确指示两种情况下的模型避免产生过于具体的假设。
见附录B中的我们的即时模板。

blocks.en:
We compare our method with the following hypothesis generation baselines: • NLParam ( Zhong et al., 2024 ) learns natural-language predicates as model parameters by optimizing a continuous relaxation of each predicate in embedding space and then prompting an LLM to verbalize it, iteratively replacing the least useful predicate. We use its classification variant with the logistic layer replaced by linear regression on IRT difficulty. • HypotheSAEs ( Movva et al., 2025 ) applies SAEs to turn the embeddings into sparse interpretable features which are then are selected via Lasso and verbalized into a hypothesis.
We obtain embeddings from the hidden-state activations of Gemma-3-4B ; because the evaluation set we use is not sufficient to finetune an SAE, we use the pretrained SAEs from Gemma-Scope-2, and have an LLM ( Gemini-3.7-Flash ) refine the verbal description of each selected feature using the questions from our dataset on which it activates. • HypoGeniC ( Zhou et al., 2024 ) generates hypotheses from labeled examples with an LLM and improves them iteratively using a bandit-style reward. As HypoGeniC is defined for classification, we adapt it to difficulty by discretizing IRT difficulty into 3 buckets and treating level prediction as the classification task. • Edisa ( Hua et al., 2023 ) is a slice detection model that discovers coherent groups of error-prone examples by fitting a mixture Gaussian model using embedding, label, and error distance. We adapt it to our setting by replacing the error distance of a single model with the IRT difficulty, and by verbalizing each discovered slice with an LLM prompted with its representative members. We set the number of slices to the hypothesis budget ℋ \mathcal{H} , and use the same embeddings as for Qwen3-Embedding-4B . In addition, to measure the predictive power of the generated hypotheses when used as features, we compare our method against a range of difficulty predictors:
(1) Fine-tuned models , for which we use RoBERTa ( Liu et al., 2019 ) , a competitive model for this task as reported in Yaneva et al. (2024) ;
(2) Frozen representations with a trained adapter, for which we take the last-token representation of Gemma-3-4B ( Kamath et al., 2025 ) and Qwen3-Embedding-4B ( Zhang et al., 2025 ) and train a Lasso regressor on top (a dense regressor would otherwise overfit as the dimension of embeddings is greater than the number of examples);
(3) Few-shot prompting of frontier LLMs, for which we use Gemini-3.1-pro-preview and Claude-Sonnet-5 .
We split the difficulty range into 5 equal-frequency buckets and randomly draw 2 questions with their answers from each bucket as demonstrations;
(4) Hypothesis-based predictors , for which we first use a judge model to determine whether each question satisfies each hypothesis as in Section 2.3 , and then train an OLS regressor on these binary features 2 2 2 More details on the datasets and the implementation of all methods are provided in Appendix C . .

blocks.zh:
我们的方法与以下假设生成基线进行比较: • NLParam(Zhong et al.,2024)通过优化嵌入空间中每个上游的连续放松,然后促使LLM进行语言化,迭代取代最不有用的上游,将自然语言上游作为模型参数学习. 我们使用它的分类变体,后勤层被ITT困难的线性回归所取代。 • 假想SAEs(Movva等人,2025年)应用SAEs将嵌入物转化为稀疏的可解释特征,然后通过拉索选择,口头化为假说.
我们从Gemma-3-4B的隐藏状态激活中获取嵌入;由于我们所用的评价集不足以微调一个SAE,所以我们使用Gemma-Scope-2的预先训练的SAE,并且有一个LLM(双子座-3.7-Flash),利用我们数据集中它激活的问题来完善对每个选定特性的口头描述. • HypoGeniC(Zhou等人,2024年)从带有LLM的标签的例子中产生假说,并使用土匪式的奖励进行反复改进. 由于HypoGeniC的定义是用于分类的,我们通过将IRT的难度磁盘化成3桶,并将水平预测作为分类任务来适应难度. • Edisa(Hua等人,2023年)是一种切片检测模型,它利用嵌入、标签和误差距离,安装混合型高斯模型,从而发现一致的易出错的例子。 我们通过用IRT困难取代单一模型的误差,用代表成员所激发的LLM对每一个发现的片段进行口头描述,来适应我们的设定。 我们设定了假设预算 H\ mathcal{H} 的切数, 并使用与 Qune3- Embedding-4B 相同的嵌入符 。 此外,为了测量所生成的假设作为特征时的预测力,我们比较了我们的方法与一系列难度预测器:
(1) 微调模型,我们使用RoBERTa(Liu等人,2019年),这是在Yaneva等人(2024年)中报告的这一任务的竞争模型;
(2) 装有训练有素的适配器的冷冻表述,我们采用Gemma-3-4B(Kamath等人,2025年)和Qune3-Embedding-4B(Zhang等人,2025年)的最后一种表达方式,并在顶部训练拉索递归器(由于嵌入的维度大于实例数,密集递归器否则会超合);
(3) 极少镜头提示边疆LLM,我们使用双子座3.1-pro-review和Claude-Sonnet-5。
我们把难度范围分成5个等频桶,随机抽出两个问题,从每个桶中解答作为演示;
(4)基于假设的预测器,我们首先使用一个判断模型来确定每个问题是否符合第2.3节中的每个假设,然后就这些二进制特征2,2,2再就数据集和所有方法的实施问题培训一个OLS递归器,详见附录C。

